  "name": "Monthly Mean Maritime Surface Weather, Physical Oceanography, and Seasonal Mean Extratropical Storms for the Northeast Pacific Ocean",
  "description": "Publication Title: Northeast Pacific Environmental Scenario. Contains monthly mean low cloud with visibility/wind speed; total cloud by wind direction; relative wet bulb humidity; fog and visibility by wind direction; precipitation types by wind direction; sea surface temperature by wind direction with wind speed; sea wave direction/period with recurrence intervals; wind direction and speed; daylight / darkness graphs and seasonal mean extratropical storms and currents. Observations used to compute this climatology span a period of more than 100 years. Most data were collected during the post World War II period until about 1974. Includes information from Ocean Weather Stations P and N. Available from the NOAA Library System: URL http://www.lib.noaa.gov/.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This publication is in the National Oceanic & Atmospheric Administration Library, and is one of many books, atlases, maps, charts and other printed materials received by NOAA from many nations over the years.",
